<title>USA: Hertz Corp sells $150 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Hertz Corp sells $150 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Hertz Corp was priced on Tuesday, according to lead manager JP Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>Hertz Corp is the world's largest car rental company.</p>
<p>BORROWER HERTZ CORP</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 5/1/2002</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.779  FIRST PAY DATE 11/1/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A3    YIELD 7.054 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD 50 BP	CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
